        "original_id": "346610ec-afc2-57e9-9072-ed0f24528cc0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jesse James, William T. Anderson\n- Organizations: James–Younger Gang\n- Places: western Missouri, Little Dixie\n- Roles: outlaw, bank robber, train robber, guerrilla leader, pro-Confederate guerrilla leader\n- Events: American Civil War\n\nFacts:\n- William T. Anderson was born in 1840 and was later known as \"Bloody Bill\" Anderson.\n- Jesse Woodson James was born on September 5, 1847, and died on April 3, 1882.\n- Jesse James was an American outlaw, bank robber, train robber, guerrilla, and leader of the James–Younger Gang.\n- Jesse James was raised in the Little Dixie area of western Missouri.\n- Jesse James and his family maintained strong Southern sympathies.\n- William T. Anderson died on October 26, 1864.\n- William T. Anderson was one of the deadliest and most brutal pro-Confederate guerrilla leaders in the American Civil War.",
